{
  "uid": "aber-gateway-health",
  "title": "Gateway Fleet Health",
  "description": "Every gateway's condition, and one appliance's in detail. Pick a gateway with the variable above.\n\nTWO DATASOURCES, AND THE SPLIT IS NOT ARBITRARY. The table and the stat tiles read `public.gateway_health` (migration 0036) on the Supabase datasource: it is authoritative, survives a daemon restart, and is what the certificate-expiry alert rule evaluates. The trend panels read labelled gauges the ingestion daemon exports to Prometheus, because the database columns hold a CURRENT VALUE AND NO HISTORY -- migration 0035 says so in its own header -- and \"is the disk filling\" is not answerable from a current value.\n\n`agent_version`, `flow_hash` and the CA expiry deliberately have no Prometheus series: that endpoint needs no credential and is published to the host, so a configuration fingerprint and the date the fleet's trust anchor dies stay in the database. ingestion/metrics.py's header carries the argument.",
  "tags": [
    "aber",
    "platform",
    "gateways"
  ],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "refresh": "30s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "gateway",
        "label": "Gateway",
        "description": "Every non-archived gateway, refreshed on dashboard load. The list SHOWS the gateway's name and PASSES its sparkplug_id, which is the immutable wire identity -- so a rename does not break a saved link, and the same value selects the Prometheus series, whose `edge_node` label is that id.",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "postgres",
          "uid": "supabase"
        },
        "definition": "SELECT gateway_name AS __text, sparkplug_id AS __value FROM gateway_health ORDER BY gateway_name",
        "query": "SELECT gateway_name AS __text, sparkplug_id AS __value FROM gateway_health ORDER BY gateway_name",
        "refresh": 1,
        "sort": 1,
        "multi": false,
        "includeAll": false,
        "hide": 0,
        "current": {},
        "options": []
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Fleet",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Every gateway, worst first",
      "description": "One row per non-archived gateway, from `public.gateway_health` (migration 0036). Sorted so anything stale, and anything whose CA is closest to expiry, is at the top.\n\n**Blank health columns are not a fault.** A host-run gateway has no appliance behind it, and a Remote one on a bundle predating migration 0035 does not report health at all -- which is why `Health age` is empty rather than large. A LARGE health age is the interesting case: the appliance is still heartbeating but its collector has stopped.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "postgres",
        "uid": "supabase"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 9,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 1
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "table",
          "rawQuery": true,
          "datasource": {
            "type": "postgres",
            "uid": "supabase"
          },
          "rawSql": "SELECT gateway_name AS \"Gateway\",\n       live_status AS \"Status\",\n       heartbeat_age_seconds AS \"Heartbeat age\",\n       health_age_seconds AS \"Health age\",\n       disk_free_bytes AS \"Disk free\",\n       mem_available_bytes AS \"Memory available\",\n       load_1m AS \"Load 1m\",\n       cert_expires_in_days AS \"CA expires in\",\n       agent_version AS \"Bundle\",\n       left(flow_hash, 12) AS \"Flow\"\n  FROM gateway_health\n ORDER BY is_stale DESC, cert_expires_in_days NULLS LAST, gateway_name"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "align": "auto",
            "cellOptions": {
              "type": "auto"
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
