      "description": "How long ago this appliance last reported any health metric.\n\n**Read the three panels above beside this one.** A Prometheus gauge holds its last value indefinitely, so a flat disk line means either a steady disk or a dead collector -- and only this series tells the two apart. It climbs at one second per second when reporting has stopped. The appliance's own flow drops host readings older than five minutes rather than republishing them.",
