    {
      "id": 15,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Clock offset",
      "description": "How far this appliance's own clock is from the platform's, in seconds. **Positive means the appliance is ahead**, which is the direction that corrupts.\n\n**This is the fault that passes every other panel on this page.** Devices supply their own metric timestamps and are trusted for ordering, so a gateway a minute fast is ONLINE, drops nothing, and files every reading a minute early -- silently and permanently. Certificate validity is measured in months, so TLS tolerates exactly the skew the historian does not.\n\nThe measurement costs the appliance nothing: ingestion subtracts the timestamp the node put on its own heartbeat from the time that heartbeat arrived. Beyond **+5 minutes** the telemetry is discarded outright rather than misfiled; the backward tolerance is a full day, because a gateway flushing a buffered outage is legitimate late data.\n\nNothing here corrects it. It is fixed on the appliance -- see docs/remote-gateways.md.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 30
